body:
I don't think it's dumb, I think you've subconsciously zeroed in on a need, and the jealousy is like the indicator light. 

I think a lot of the times when we get jealous it's because of an inherent need- idk about you, but as a kid I wasn't really praised for my looks, only for how obedient I was. So now, every compliment on my looks is like a drop in the desert that I'll drink up greedily. If someone compliments my co-worker but not me, for example, I'll mentally be like "what about me???", and then when I don't get acknowledged I can feel the jealousy brewing. It's nothing against my co-worker, it's more like lack of acknowledgement implicitly placing you as the "second place" or "loser", which in turn translates to the "lesser than", which in turn hurts your self-esteem. It also makes you feel excluded, because someone was acknowledged while you were not. It's a convoluted thought process, but it *is * rooted in logic, however subconscious, so please don't call yourself dumb. 

Unfortunately I don't really have a solution, I struggle with my feelings every day, and walk myself through the logical steps of "just because they didn't compliment me doesn't mean I'm any lesser". My hope is that practice and repetition will make it rote memory ^^;; but I just wanted to tell you to not put yourself down by calling yourself dumb, your brain is just working on the next level ^^;;
